course: dictionary
lesson: 15340
title: Softness: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Softness is a noun, and it is a word you can use in many different ways. The meaning changes with the words around it. «The softness of the kitten's fur made Maya smile.» Here the clue is fur and smiling, so softness means how gently something feels when you touch it.
explain: Read the context for sound and light too. «The softness of candlelight made the room feel calm.» Candlelight is not something you touch, so softness must mean quiet and gentle. Ask yourself: what is being described? Then try your meaning in the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Softness can also describe a person. «He had a softness of heart, and he always helped the lost puppies.» Helping others shows gentleness and kindness. Be careful, though: «His softness meant the class got away with too much» shows that softness can mean being too weak or not strict enough. The clues tell you which meaning is right.
fact: Softness is a noun, and it is uncountable: you say the softness, not softnesses.
fact: «Softness» can mean how soft something feels to touch, such as a pillow or a kitten's fur.
fact: «Softness» can mean quiet or gentle sound or light, such as «the softness of her voice».
fact: In science, softness is a property of materials: a material is soft if it is easily scratched or squashed. Chalk is soft; granite is hard.
fact: «Softness» can mean gentleness and kindness in a person, but it can also mean being too weak or not strict enough.
exercise: «The softness of the kitten's fur made Maya smile.» What does softness mean here? | How fast something moves | How heavy something is | *How soft something feels to touch | How loud a sound is
exercise: In science, a material has softness if it is what? | *Easily scratched or squashed | Always shiny and bright | Made only of metal | Very tall and thin
exercise: «He had a softness of heart, and he always helped the lost puppies.» What does softness mean here? | Brightness of colour | Loudness of voice | Weakness in the legs | *Gentleness and kindness
test: «The softness of candlelight made the room feel calm.» What does softness describe? | Hardness of the walls | Heavy noise | *Quiet, gentle light | Speed of the flame
test: «His softness meant the class got away with too much.» What might softness mean here? | Being a fast runner | Strength and firm rules | *Being too weak or not strict enough | Shouting loudly
exam: Which meaning fits best in «The softness of her voice calmed the baby»? | *Quiet and gentle sound | Fast and busy movement | Bright, flashing light | Hard and rough texture
